ABOUT THIS PROJECT

QoL Compendium takes quality of life mods that have not been updated for the
current build of Project Zomboid and rebuilds them, as a single mod. Most of it
is written from scratch against the current game rather than copied, because
build 41 code generally does not survive the move to build 42 intact.


THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

Everything here is original work except where listed below. Where a component
is bundled, it remains the property of its author and is not covered by this
project's licence.

  Adrenaline
    From "Adrenaline - Panic Counters Tiredness", Steam Workshop 2807001835.
    Stated terms: MIT, declared by the author in the mod description.

    Bundled: no files. The implementation was written for this project, because
    the original reads and writes fatigue through methods build 42 removed.

    Taken: the mechanic and its balance values, meaning the absorption caps per
    panic level, the rates and the crash multiplier. Those numbers are the
    author's judgement rather than ours, and MIT covers their reuse.

    The mod ships no licence file and names no author in mod.info, so no
    copyright line is reproduced here. The Workshop page above identifies the
    author.

  Ammo and Magazine Icons
    Workshop 1904952813, by falcon33jp
    Stated terms: none.

    Bundled: twelve inventory icons for ammo boxes and magazines. Build 42
    draws five handgun ammo boxes with one icon, three rifle boxes with
    another and three pistol magazines with a third, so these give each item
    its own. Artwork cannot be reimplemented from a description, so unlike the
    rest of this project these files are the originals.

    Not taken: the loose ammo icons and every world model. Vanilla's are fine.
    The code that applies them was written for this project.

  Rifle Sling
    Models and textures: Akyet
    Hotbar and attachment code: Noir
    From "Actual Realistic Rifle Sling", Steam Workshop 3073937977, itself a
    modification of Noir's Rifle Sling.

    Bundled: two sling models, its texture and icon, two clothing item
    definitions, and the hotbar attachment logic. A 3D model cannot be
    reimplemented from a description, so unlike the rest of this project these
    files are the originals. Two of the original's four wearing styles were
    dropped, and the files renamed, but the models themselves are unmodified.

    Rewritten for this project: the crafting recipe, which used build 41's
    "recipe" format that build 42 no longer supports at all, and the spawn
    distribution.

    No licence or permission statement was published with the original.

Components adapted in concept only, sharing no files or code with their source,
are listed in README.md.


ASSETS GENERATED FOR THIS PROJECT

The moodle overlay textures are produced procedurally by
tools/generate_overlays.py and share no pixels with any other mod.


